979:
The public health, safety, morals and general welfare require that substructions meet certain standards. Sub-standard structures can create severe problems that the city has a duty to attempt to prevent. In furtherance of this purpose, this ordinance [appendix] is adopted to:
(a) Decrease the hazard fire, accidents or other calamities;
(b) Assure that all structures provide adequate ventilation, light and sanitary facilities;
(c) Address dilapidation or disrepair due to the owner's failure to maintain the premises;
(d) Address structural defects that render a structure unsafe for human habitation or occupancy; and
(e) Address uncleanness that creates a health hazard for others in the community.
